# Bundled One True Awk source

Origin: NetBSD pkgsrc, with EmberBSD adaptations (AI-assisted).

../SOURCE.json pins the official tagged snapshot and its archive bytes.
Upstream does not normally make formal releases. The selected tag is 20260426.
The upstream copyright, LICENSE, FIXES and FIXES.1e remain in this bundle.
README.md is named README. awk.1 is named nawk.1 and uses the installed command.
The book title and upstream language names remain unchanged.

The lib.c byte classification casts retain the NetBSD repair from commit
7099c72bfddcbf9671d3a3478636cf05e73bbfaa (Roland Illig, 2025-07-26).
They also cover the new hexadecimal check and existing variable-name checks.
Two new format-width byte checks in run.c use the same unsigned-char rule.
Wide-character classification keeps its upstream behavior.

The bootstrap script copies lang/nawk/files. The ordinary recipe extracts the
same files. The Makefile uses the bundled parser and procedure table, without
running a host generator during either build. CC, CFLAGS and LDFLAGS remain
explicit producer selections. No old parser output can enter a new bundle.

Upstream defaults to Bison. The BSD bundled integration uses a selected,
pinned byacc to prepare awkgram.tab.c and awkgram.tab.h. The selected GCC16
builds upstream maketab.c to prepare proctab.c. Both are source preparation,
not target programs. See ../regenerate.py. Its private record captures tool
hashes and exact argv. Generated files and their source hashes must pass the
source gate before publication. Runtime and compiler acceptance are separate.

The complete testdir and bugs-fixed cases remain upstream inputs. The testdir
harness requires explicit CC, awk and oldawk selections and honors compiler
and linker flags for its echo helper. It does not select a host cc or awk.

CC names one selected compiler executable. Pass arguments separately through
CPPFLAGS, CFLAGS and LDFLAGS. Do not place compiler flags or a command tuple
in CC. The derived Makefile retains the full upstream Lucent license notice.

The split() memory adaptation reuses checked tostring() for source/separator
copies. The CSV scratch buffer includes a NUL byte and checks allocation
failure with FATAL. The source gate verifies this exact upstream adaptation.
